hadiths[102]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4188","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fatimah is a part of me, so whoever angers her has angered me."
"4189","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fatimah is a part of me; what distresses her distresses me, and what gladdens her gladdens me. Indeed, on the Day of Resurrection all lineages will be cut off except my lineage, my ties and my relationship by marriage."
"4190","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fatimah is the leader of the women of Paradise, except for Maryam bint Imran."
"4191","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has opened a door for repentance toward the west, the width of which is a journey of seventy years. It will not be closed until the sun rises from that direction."
"4192","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Today an opening like this has been made in the barrier of Ya'juj and Ma'juj (Gog and Magog)"" - and he (peace and blessings be upon him) formed the number ninety with his hand."
"4193","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The revelation stopped coming to me for a period. Then one day, while I was walking, I heard a voice from the sky, so I raised my gaze toward the sky, and there was the same angel who had come to me in the cave of Hira, sitting on a throne between the sky and the earth. I was so frightened of him that I fell to the ground. Then I came to Khadijah and said: 'Cover me, cover me.' So she covered me. Then Jibril came and said: 'O you who are wrapped in a garment! Arise and warn, and magnify your Lord, and keep your garments pure, and keep away from filth.'"
"4194","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The trial of al-Ahlas is flight and war. Then comes the trial of al-Sarra', whose smoke will rise from beneath the feet of a man from my household; he will claim that he is from me, yet he is not from me, for my friends are only the God-fearing. Then the people will settle upon a man like a hip on a rib. Then comes the trial of al-Duhayma', which will not leave anyone of this Ummah without striking him a slap. When it is said that it is over, it will drag on further. In it a man will be a believer in the morning and a disbeliever by evening, until the people are divided into two camps: a camp of faith in which there is no hypocrisy, and a camp of hypocrisy in which there is no faith. So when that happens, expect the Dajjal that very day or the next."
"4195","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A man's trial concerning his family, his wealth, his own self, his children and his neighbour is wiped away by fasting, prayer, charity, enjoining good and forbidding evil."
"4196","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Four rivers flow from Paradise: the Euphrates, the Nile, Sayhan and Jayhan."
"4197","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The thigh of a Muslim man is part of his 'awrah (what must be covered)."
"4198","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""One bed is for the man, one bed for his wife, the third for the guest, and the fourth is for Satan."
"4199","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The roof of my house was opened while I was in Makkah, and Jibril descended. He split open my chest, then washed it with Zamzam water. Then he brought a golden basin full of wisdom and faith, poured it into my chest, and then closed it up. Then he took me by the hand and ascended with me to the lowest heaven. When we reached the lowest heaven, Jibril said to the gatekeeper of the lowest heaven: Open. He asked: Who is this? Jibril said: This is Jibril. He asked: Is anyone with you? Jibril said: Yes, Muhammad is with me. He asked: Has he been sent for? Jibril said: Yes, so open. When we ascended the lowest heaven, there was a man with some shadowy figures on his right and some shadowy figures on his left; when he looked to his right he laughed, and when he looked to his left he wept. He said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous son! I asked: O Jibril, who is this? He said: This is Adam, and these shadowy figures on his right and his left are the souls of his descendants. Those on the right are the people of Paradise, and the shadowy figures on his left are the people of the Fire; so when he looks to his right he laughs, and when he looks to his left he weeps. Then Jibril ascended with me until he reached the second heaven, and he said to its gatekeeper: Open. Its gatekeeper said the same as the gatekeeper of the lowest heaven had said, and then he opened. When I passed by Idris, he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother! I asked: Who is this? Jibril said: This is Idris. Then I passed by Musa, and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother! I asked: Who is this? Jibril said: This is Musa. Then I passed by Isa, and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous brother! I asked: Who is this? Jibril said: This is Isa, son of Maryam. Then I passed by Ibrahim, and he said: Welcome to the righteous Prophet and the righteous son! I asked: Who is this? Jibril said: This is Ibrahim. Then I was taken up until I reached a height where I heard the scratching of the pens. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, made fifty prayers obligatory upon my Ummah. I returned with that until I passed by Musa. Musa asked: What has your Lord made obligatory upon your Ummah? I said: He has made fifty prayers obligatory upon them. Musa said to me: Go back to your Lord, for your Ummah will not be able to bear that. So I went back to my Lord, and He reduced it by half. Then I returned to Musa and told him, and he said: Go back to your Lord, for your Ummah will not be able to bear even that. So I went back to my Lord again, and He said: They are five, and they are fifty in reward; the word does not change with Me. So I returned to Musa, and he said: Go back to your Lord. I said: I now feel shy before my Lord. Then I was taken on until I reached the Lote Tree of the Utmost Boundary (Sidrat al-Muntaha). Its fruits were like the earthen jars of Hajar, and its leaves were like the ears of elephants; a single leaf would almost cover this Ummah. It was covered by colours that I do not know what they were. Then I was admitted into Paradise, and in it were domes of pearl, and its soil was musk."
"4200","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Four things have been decreed for the son of Adam: his creation, his character, his provision and his appointed time of death."
"4201","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has decreed five things for every servant: his appointed time of death, his provision, his footsteps, his resting place, and whether he is wretched or blessed."
"4202","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has decreed five things for every servant: his deeds, his appointed time of death, his provision, his footsteps and his resting place."
"4203","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah has decreed four things: creation, character, provision and the appointed time of death."
"4204","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah decreed the measures (of all things) and the affairs of this world fifty thousand years before He created the heavens and the earth."
"4205","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the day of the Great Battle, the main camp of the Muslims will be in a land called al-Ghutah, in which there is a city called Damascus; it will be the best dwelling place of the Muslims on that day."
"4206","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The distinction between what is lawful and what is unlawful is the beating of the daff and the voice (of celebration) at a marriage."
"4207","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The distinction between our fasting and the fasting of the People of the Book is the pre-dawn meal (suhur)."
"4208","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah favoured Quraysh with seven qualities: He favoured them in that they worshipped Allah for ten years when no one but Quraysh worshipped Allah; He favoured them in that He helped them on the Day of the Elephant while they were idolaters; He favoured them in that a surah of the Qur'an was revealed about them in which no one else in the worlds is included, and that is 'For the familiarity of Quraysh'; and He favoured them in that among them are prophethood, the caliphate, the custodianship of the Ka'bah (hijabah) and the provision of water to the pilgrims (siqayah)."
"4209","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah favoured Quraysh with seven qualities that were not given to anyone before them and will not be given to anyone after them: Allah favoured Quraysh in that I am from them; that prophethood is among them; that the custodianship of the Ka'bah (hijabah) is among them; that the provision of water to the pilgrims (siqayah) is among them; that He helped them against the people of the Elephant; that they worshipped Allah for ten years when no one besides them worshipped Him; and that Allah revealed about them a surah of the Qur'an in which no one besides them is mentioned: 'For the familiarity of Quraysh.'"
"4210","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The superiority of Aishah over other women is like the superiority of tharid over all other food."
"4211","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The virtue of prayer in al-Masjid al-Haram over other mosques is equal to one hundred thousand prayers, and the virtue of prayer in my mosque is equal to one thousand prayers."
"4212","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The superiority of the scholar over the worshipper is like the superiority of the moon on the night of the full moon over all the other stars."
"4213","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The superiority of the scholar over the worshipper is like my superiority over the lowest of you. Indeed, Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, His angels, and the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth, even the ant in its hole and even the fish, send blessings upon the one who teaches people what is good."
"4214","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The virtue of knowledge is more beloved to me than the virtue of worship, and the best of your religion is scrupulous piety."
"4215","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The superiority of prayer in congregation over a man's prayer alone is twenty-five degrees."
"4216","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The superiority of prayer in congregation over the prayer of one alone is twenty-five degrees, and the angels of the night and the angels of the day gather at the Fajr prayer."
"4217","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The superiority of a man's prayer in his house over his prayer where people can see him is like the superiority of the obligatory prayer over the voluntary one."
"4218","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The superiority of Aishah over other women is like the superiority of tharid over all other food."
"4219","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been favoured with four things: I and my Ummah have been made to form rows in prayer as the angels form rows; the earth has been made a means of ablution for me; the ground has been made for me a place of prostration and a means of purification; and the spoils of war have been made lawful for me."
"4220","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been favoured with four things: the earth has been made for me a place of prostration and a means of purification, so whichever man of my Ummah comes to the prayer and finds nothing to pray upon will find the earth a place of prostration and a means of purification; I have been sent to all people; I have been helped by awe cast (into the enemy) at a distance of two months' journey, which goes ahead of me; and the spoils of war have been made lawful for me."
"4221","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been favoured over the Prophets with five things: I have been sent to all people; I have kept my intercession in reserve for my Ummah; I have been helped by awe cast (into the enemy) at a distance of a month's journey ahead of me and a month's journey behind me; the earth has been made for me a place of prostration and a means of purification; and the spoils of war have been made lawful for me, which were not made lawful for anyone before me."
"4222","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I have been favoured over the Prophets with six things: I have been given concise, comprehensive speech; I have been helped by awe cast (into the enemy); the spoils of war have been made lawful for me; the earth has been made for me a means of purification and a place of prostration; I have been sent to all of creation; and the line of Prophets has been sealed with me."
"4223","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""We have been favoured over the people with three things: our rows have been made like the rows of the angels; the whole earth has been made a place of prostration for us; its soil has been made a means of purification for us when we do not find water; and I have been given these verses at the end of Surah al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne, which were not given to any Prophet before me."
"4224","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your Eid al-Fitr is the day on which you break the fast, your Eid al-Adha is the day on which you offer your sacrifices, and Arafah is the day on which you stand at Arafah."
"4225","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Your Eid al-Fitr is the day on which you break the fast, and your Eid al-Adha is the day on which you offer your sacrifices. The whole of Arafah is a place of standing, the whole of Mina is a place of sacrifice, all the pathways of Makkah are a place of sacrifice, and the whole of Muzdalifah is a place of standing."
"4226","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Doing good protects against an evil death."
"4227","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A community of the Children of Israel went missing, and it is not known what became of it, and I do not think it is anything but the rat. Do you not see that when camel's milk is placed before it, it does not drink, but when sheep's milk is placed before it, it drinks?"
"4228","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The poor among the Muhajirun will enter Paradise five hundred years before their wealthy."
"4229","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Free the captive, accept the invitation of the one who invites, feed the hungry and visit the sick."
"4230","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Then who infected the first one?"
"4231","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The passing away of my Ummah will be by spear wounds and by plague, and it (the plague) is the piercing of your enemies from among the jinn, and in each there is martyrdom."
"4232","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fulfil (your covenant) with them, and we will seek the help of Allah against them."
"4233","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Why did you not marry a virgin, with whom you would play and who would play with you, and with whom you would laugh and who would laugh with you?"
"4234","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In one of the wings of a fly there is poison and in the other there is cure. So when it falls into food, dip it in, for it puts the poison forward and keeps the cure back."
"4235","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Among my Companions there are twelve hypocrites; eight of them will not enter Paradise until a camel passes through the eye of a needle."
"4236","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For camels there is a fara', and for sheep there is a fara'; an aqiqah is offered for a boy, and his head is not to be touched with blood."
"4237","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For the teeth, the blood money for each is five camels."
"4238","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For the fingers, the blood money for each is ten camels."
"4239","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In a human being there are three hundred and sixty joints, so he must give a charity on behalf of each joint: burying spittle in the mosque, and removing something from the road, are also charity. If you are unable to do that, then the two rak'ahs of the Duha prayer will suffice for you."
"4240","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For the nose, if it is cut off completely, there is the full blood money, one hundred camels; for a hand, fifty; for a foot, fifty; for an eye, fifty; for an ammah (a head wound reaching the brain's membrane), one third of the full blood money; for a ja'ifah (a wound penetrating the body cavity), one third of the full blood money; for a munaqqilah (a wound displacing a bone), fifteen camels; for a mudihah (a wound exposing the bone), five camels; for a tooth, five camels; and for each finger, ten camels."
"4241","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there is a gate called al-Rayyan, through which those who fast will be called. Whoever is among those who fast will enter through it, and whoever enters through it will never be thirsty."
"4242","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Paradise has eight gates; among them is a gate called al-Rayyan, through which none will enter except those who fast."
"4243","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there is a tent made of a hollow pearl, sixty miles wide. In each of its corners there will be family members who will not be able to see one another, and the believer will go round to visit them all in turn."
"4244","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there are one hundred levels; between every two levels is a distance like that between the heaven and the earth. Al-Firdaws is the highest level among them; from it the four rivers of Paradise gush forth, and above it is the Throne. So when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws."
"4245","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there are one hundred levels; between every two levels is a distance of one hundred years."
"4246","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there is that which no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and has never occurred to the heart of any human being."
"4247","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the black seed (kalonji) there is a cure for every disease except sam (death)."
"4248","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In cupping there is a cure."
"4249","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On one of the fly's wings there is disease and on the other there is a cure. So when it falls into a vessel, submerge it, and its cure will remove its disease."
"4250","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On buried treasure (rikaz) there is one fifth."
"4251","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For (hunting) a hyena, (the penalty) is a ram."
"4252","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On honey, for every ten skins, one skin is due as zakah."
"4253","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""With a boy there is an aqiqah, so shed blood on his behalf and remove the harm from him."
"4254","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In (serving) every thirsting liver there is reward."
"4255","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the hypocrite there are three traits: when he speaks he lies, when he makes a promise he breaks it, and when he is entrusted he betrays the trust."
"4256","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For wounds that expose the bone (mudihah), the blood money for each one is five camels."
"4257","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In my Ummah there will be (the punishments of) sinking into the earth, disfigurement of forms, and pelting with stones."
"4258","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In my Ummah there will be twenty-seven lying dajjals (impostors), among them four women; and I am the Seal of the Prophets, there is no prophet after me."
"4259","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In the tribe of Thaqif there will arise a great liar and a destructive tyrant."
"4260","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For thirty cows, a one-year-old male or female calf is due as zakah, and for forty cows, a two-year-old cow."
"4261","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For five camels there is one goat, for ten two goats, for fifteen three goats, for twenty four goats, and for twenty-five a one-year-old she-camel (bint makhad), up to thirty-five. Then if there is one more, there is a two-year-old she-camel (bint labun), up to forty-five. Then if there is one more, there is a three-year-old she-camel (hiqqah), up to sixty. Then if there is one more, there is a four-year-old she-camel (jadha'ah), up to seventy-five. Then if there is one more, there are two bint labun, up to ninety. Then if there is one more, there are two hiqqahs, up to one hundred and twenty. Then if the camels are more than that, for every fifty there is one hiqqah and for every forty one bint labun. So if they reach one hundred and twenty-one, there are three bint labun, up to one hundred and twenty-nine. Then if they reach one hundred and thirty, there are two bint labun and one hiqqah, up to one hundred and thirty-nine. Then if they reach one hundred and forty, there are two hiqqahs and one bint labun, up to one hundred and forty-nine. Then if they reach one hundred and fifty, there are three hiqqahs, up to one hundred and fifty-nine. Then if they reach one hundred and sixty, there are four bint labun, up to one hundred and sixty-nine. Then if they reach one hundred and seventy, there are three bint labun and one hiqqah, up to one hundred and seventy-nine. Then if they reach one hundred and eighty, there are two hiqqahs and two bint labun, up to one hundred and eighty-nine. Then if they reach one hundred and ninety, there are three hiqqahs and one bint labun, up to one hundred and ninety-nine. Then if they reach two hundred, there are four hiqqahs or five bint labun; whichever age of camel is available, that will be taken. And for grazing sheep and goats, for every forty there is one goat, up to one hundred and twenty. Then if there is one more, there are two goats, up to two hundred. Then if they exceed two hundred, there are three goats, up to three hundred. Then if the goats are more than that, for every hundred there is one goat. For fewer than one hundred there is nothing until they reach one hundred. And for fear of the charity, combined property is not to be separated and separate property is not to be combined; and whatever belongs to two partners, they shall settle the zakah between themselves equally. And in charity no decrepit animal is to be taken, nor a defective goat, nor the breeding he-goat of the flock, unless the zakah collector himself wishes."
"4262","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The Ajwah dates of al-Aliyah, eaten early in the morning on an empty stomach, are a cure for every magic or poison."
"4263","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In (serving) every creature with a thirsting liver there is reward."
"4264","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In every two rak'ahs there is the tahiyyat."
"4265","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In every herd of grazing camels, for forty camels there is one bint labun; the camels shall not be separated from their count. Whoever gives it seeking reward will have its reward, and whoever withholds it, we will take it along with half of his wealth; this is one of the firm commands of our Lord, the Mighty and Majestic. Nothing of it is for Muhammad or the family of Muhammad."
"4266","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In every flock of grazing sheep and goats there is a fara', which you raise along with your livestock, until when it becomes able to bear a load so that it can serve the pilgrims, you slaughter it and give its meat in charity to the wayfarer; that is better."
"4267","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In every era of my Ummah there will be those who race ahead in goodness."
"4268","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On the night of the fifteenth of Sha'ban, Allah forgives the people of the earth, except for a polytheist or one who harbours enmity."
"4269","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For fewer than twenty-five camels, there is one goat for every five. So when they reach twenty-five, there is a one-year-old she-camel (bint makhad), up to thirty-five; and if a bint makhad is not available, a male ibn labun will be taken. Then if they reach thirty-six, there is a two-year-old she-camel (bint labun), up to forty-five. Then if they reach forty-six, there is a three-year-old she-camel (hiqqah), fit for the stallion, up to sixty. Then if they reach sixty-one, there is a four-year-old she-camel (jadha'ah), up to seventy-five. Then if they reach seventy-six, there are two bint labun, up to ninety. Then if they reach ninety-one, there are two hiqqahs, fit for the stallion, up to one hundred and twenty. Then if they exceed one hundred and twenty, for every forty there is one bint labun and for every fifty one hiqqah. And if the ages of the camels do not exactly match what is obligatory in charity, then whoever owes a jadha'ah in charity and does not have a jadha'ah but has a hiqqah, it will be accepted from him, and along with it he shall give two goats, if they are easily available to him, or twenty dirhams. And whoever owes a hiqqah in charity and has nothing but a jadha'ah, it will be accepted from him and the zakah collector will give him back twenty dirhams or two goats. And whoever owes a hiqqah in charity and does not have the charity of a bint labun and has only a hiqqah, it will be accepted from him and the zakah collector will give him back twenty dirhams or two goats. And whoever owes a bint labun in charity and does not have a bint labun but has a bint makhad, it will be accepted from him, and along with it he shall give two goats, if they are easily available to him, or twenty dirhams. And whoever's charity reaches a bint makhad and he has nothing but a male ibn labun, it will be accepted from him and nothing further will be taken with it. And whoever has only four camels, there is nothing due on them unless their owner himself wishes. And in the charity of sheep and goats, when the grazing ones number forty, there is one goat, up to one hundred and twenty. Then if they are more, there are two goats, up to two hundred. Then if there is one more, there are three goats, up to three hundred. Then if they are more, for every hundred there is one goat. And in charity no decrepit animal is to be taken, nor a defective one, nor a breeding he-goat, unless the zakah collector himself wishes. And for fear of the charity, separate property is not to be combined and combined property is not to be separated; and whatever belongs to two partners, they shall settle between themselves equally. And if a man's grazing goats are one short of forty, there is nothing due on them unless their owner himself wishes. And on silver there is one fortieth as zakah; so if the wealth is no more than one hundred and ninety dirhams, there is nothing due on it unless its owner himself wishes."
"4270","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On what is watered by rain, rivers and springs, or grows by itself, there is one tenth; and on what is irrigated by buckets or by camels, there is one twentieth."
"4271","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On what is watered by rain, rivers and springs there is one tenth, and on what is irrigated with buckets there is one twentieth."
"4272","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""On what is watered by rain and springs there is one tenth, and on what is irrigated with buckets there is one twentieth."
"4273","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In this Ummah there will be (the punishments of) sinking into the earth, disfigurement of forms, and pelting with stones, when singing slave-girls and musical instruments become widespread and wines are drunk."
"4274","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""In this Ummah there will be (the punishments of) sinking into the earth, disfigurement of forms, and pelting with stones upon the deniers of predestination."
"4275","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Strive (make jihad) in serving the two of them."
"4276","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who flees from the plague is like one who flees from the battlefield, and the one who remains patient in it is like one who remains steadfast on the battlefield."
"4277","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The one who flees from the plague is like one who flees from the battlefield, and whoever remains patient in it will have the reward of a martyr."
"4278","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dawn (fajr) is of two kinds: the dawn that is like the tail of a wolf, in which the prayer does not become permissible nor does food become forbidden; and the dawn that spreads out lengthwise across the horizon, in which the prayer becomes permissible and food becomes forbidden."
"4279","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dawn (fajr) is of two kinds: a dawn in which food becomes forbidden and the prayer becomes permissible, and a dawn in which the prayer is forbidden and food is permissible."
"4280","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The thigh is part of the awrah (what must be covered)."
"4281","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Pride and arrogance are found among the owners of camels, and tranquility and dignity among the owners of sheep and goats."
"4282","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fleeing from the plague is like fleeing from the battlefield."
"4283","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Al-Firdaws is the height of Paradise, its highest and its middle part, and from it the rivers of Paradise gush forth."
"4284","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The fara' is a right; but if you leave it until it becomes a half-grown young camel, one or two years old, and then give it to a widow or give it as a mount in the path of Allah, that is better than slaughtering it at a young age, so that its flesh sticks to its hair, and you overturn your vessel, and you make your she-camel distraught."
"4285","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Silver for silver, gold for gold, barley for barley, and wheat for wheat, like for like."
"4286","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eid al-Fitr is the day on which you break the fast, and Eid al-Adha is the day on which you offer the sacrifice."
"4287","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Eid al-Fitr is the day on which the people break the fast, and Eid al-Adha is the day on which the people offer the sacrifice."
"4288","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The practices of the fitrah (natural disposition) are clipping the nails, trimming the moustache, and shaving the pubic hair."
"4289","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Understanding of the religion (fiqh) is from Yemen, and wisdom too is Yemeni."
